{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## FINAL REPORT — rebar-debug\n\n### Problem\nThe DC harness errored all 62 live cells at fixture setup, blocking epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb]'s\n14th criterion.\n\n### Proven root cause — an ORDERING DEADLOCK, not a budget shortfall\nGreenHopper provisions `Epic Link`/`Epic Name` **when the first Jira Software project is\ncreated**, not when the plugin starts. [rebar:9790-cafa-dffa-462e] made those fields a\nSESSION-START readiness predicate, so the gate waited for a capability only the action it\nblocked could produce. `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` + `conftest.py::wait_for_jira_dc_ready`.\n\n### Proof — experiment 30981084637\n    [before]            27 fields, customfield_count=0, EpicLink=False\n    [after-180s-quiet]  27 fields, customfield_count=0, EpicLink=False   <- TIME alone: no change\n    create project -> HTTP 201\n    [after-create+0s]   55 fields, customfield_count=13, EpicLink=True   <- ACTION: 0.0512s\nThe quiet-settle leg is the discriminator: it supplied time WITHOUT the action.\nAlternatives killed: **budget** (600s and 1800s expired with byte-identical inventories, runs\n30975323866/30978613228, container idle ~29 min after `Startup is complete`); **genuine\ndegrade** and **name mismatch** (run 30964805133 passed 62/62 on this image including\n`test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link`).\n\n### Live verification — run **30982731669**, jira DC harness job: **62 passed, 1 xfailed in 2552.64s**\n**0 failed, 0 errored.** Identical shape to the last-known-green 30964805133.\nThe measurement now appears 57 times in that log, once per scratch project:\n    [941b-field-readiness] project RBJOQYL: Epic field(s) ['Epic Link', 'Epic Name'] registered\n    after 1 poll(s) in 0.058s; resolved ids {'Epic Link': 'customfield_10008',\n    'Epic Name': 'customfield_10004'}\nObserved range **0.032s-0.058s**, always 1 poll — corroborating the 0.0512s the 120s allowance\nis sized from.\n\n**The workflow RUN is red, and it is not this change.** Only `external LLM (live bedrock)`\nfailed: `Not authorized to perform sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`. Verified against history —\nbedrock SUCCEEDS on `main` (30964805133, 30975323866) and FAILS on `scratch-941b-probe`\n(30978613228, 30982731669). The AWS OIDC trust policy is ref-scoped, so that arm cannot pass on\na branch. It will not occur once this lands on main.\n\n### Gates\n- Gerrit **1421** patchset 2: **Verified +1**. LLM-Review PASSED **+1** on patchset 1 with 3\n  advisory (non-blocking) findings; the vote reset on patchset 2 and is re-running.\n- `make lint` **exit 0**, `make typecheck` **exit 0** (434 files).\n- `pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -n 4 --dist worksteal -q`:\n  **1 failed, 10333 passed, 38 skipped**. The one failure is [rebar:78f4-8cc7-bc8c-4ac2],\n  proven pre-existing on a clean worktree at origin/main.\n\n### A gate this change tripped, caught locally\n`test_comment_hygiene_guard::test_the_real_tree_is_clean` failed on 4 bare CI run ids in new\ncomments — the guard requires a resolvable ticket id in the same comment block. Fixed by citing\n`941b-f049-5f29-4410` in each; `check_comment_hygiene.py` now exits 0. Also worth recording: an\nearlier suite run showed 8 spurious ERRORs, all \"Test moved the repo HEAD\" — caused by my own\nrebase/amend running CONCURRENTLY with pytest. They vanished in a clean serialized re-run. Do\nnot run git history operations while the suite is running.\n\n### Siblings (Step 7)\n- **Construct sweep** — the class is 'a pre-flight wait for a capability provisioned by the\n  action it blocks'. One live sibling found and fixed in scope: the deterministic probe\n  (`scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py`), whose `_await_named_fields` ran before its\n  project create — which is why probe runs 30944211742 and 30930839323 have BOTH failed at\n  `PROBE SETUP FAILED` since 1387 'fixed' that path. Every other bounded wait in the tier is\n  action-then-wait and therefore correct: `_poll_until_404` (DELETE then poll),\n  `test_llm_trace.py` (`force_flush()` then poll), and stage 1 serverInfo (the container\n  produces it independently of the suite).\n- **Parity census** — rule: *the Epic-field check must run after a Software project exists*.\n  CLI **N/A**; MCP/API **N/A**; library facade **N/A** (`scripts/` module, not exported from\n  `rebar`); automated callers **2 of 2 fixed** (harness `_assert_project_capabilities`, probe\n  `_await_named_fields`), both still routing through the one shared `await_required_fields`;\n  dual-direction — the failure side (`not_ready_message`) was already shared but the success\n  side was NOT, so the two tiers reported a successful wait differently; `ready_message` closes\n  that. Two other `/rest/api/2/field` readers checked and cleared:\n  `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` (agentic checklist, not a blocking gate) and\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py` (write-time discovery that DECLINES rather than\n  waits).\n\n### Residual risk\n- **ticket filed** [rebar:ccf6-a065-b1d6-4cf1] — `live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is 932 LOC, over the\n  800 hard cap (917 before this change; the enforced CI gate covers `src/rebar` only).\n- **ticket filed** [rebar:78f4-8cc7-bc8c-4ac2] — the pre-existing red cell in the marker suite.\n- **fixed in scope** — 9790's refuted decision rule; also recorded as a correction comment on\n  [rebar:9790-cafa-dffa-462e] itself, since that ticket is where the next reader will look.\n\n### Replication\nThe original report no longer reproduces: the reported scenario is the harness job itself, and\nit is green end to end with 0 failed and 0 errored cells (run 30982731669).\n\n**Not closing this ticket** — handing to the operator to verify against the acceptance criteria."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785915971918505001,"uuid":"194d58c4-7b12-4021-bdf1-48087a849c96"}